        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "_freeze_side"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-15WP0QCN",
      "invariant": "INV-9BH2BNCT",
      "origin": {
        "leaf": "260921-ICR-L46"
      },
      "rationale": "Copies one knowledge half into the stage through the snapshot owner. For a recovery parent it first requires the half to be recorded as retained with the exact identity now read. A moved half or a snapshot that cannot be opened returns a named refusal rather than being bound as an ordinary absent side.",
      "role": "enforcement"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "87c7c5dcefcbaf93baf68a0c8eec34ad2dd11703",
        "content": "sha256:bfebbf86142444834662aa0477abc0ba4e42a907f9e843f2df380e167e1dffd6",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "_retained_capture"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-A54M1HGQ",
      "invariant": "INV-9BH2BNCT",
      "origin": {
        "leaf": "260921-ICR-L46"
      },
      "rationale": "Revalidates custody of the explicitly selected historical capture. The resolution must be that exact parent generation, the manifest re-read from disk must still match its recorded digest and the reopened manifest, and the resolved code trees and root must equal the manifest's recorded source. Only then does it return the recorded candidate capture as retained input, never as a live one.",
      "role": "enforcement"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "87c7c5dcefcbaf93baf68a0c8eec34ad2dd11703",
        "content": "sha256:b32365c75a1f16a9cd2daaeef9fd447f4def91254371b53ccba604d104e7108e",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "_side_binding"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-D2SEVSM9",
      "invariant": "INV-9BH2BNCT",
      "origin": {
        "leaf": "260921-ICR-L46"
      },
      "rationale": "Decides each knowledge half's binding. If the half's dataset file is missing while the parent manifest recorded it as retained, it refuses 'the expected retained snapshot disappeared' instead of falling through to the ordinary absent-side binding; otherwise it binds absence, refuses a contradicted declared absence, or freezes the half.",
      "role": "enforcement"
    }
  ],
